GLOSSARY — real-world-donated vocabulary, ready to use as-is or adapt

Everything here is real terminology pulled from the actual research (not invented for this project). Listed
with a plain-language gloss and its most natural in-religion use.

---

ANA / KATA
Real 1880s coinage (Charles Hinton). The two new directions a fourth spatial dimension would add, playing
the same role "up"/"down" plays for the third dimension we already have. Could be used directly as
liturgical/directional vocabulary — "moving ana," "the kata-ward path," etc. — without needing translation
or adaptation.

SPISSITUDE
Real 1671 coinage (Henry More). Proposed "hyperthickness" in the fourth dimension distinguishing a living
body from a dead one — invisible from ordinary 3D space, but physically real in the theory. Strong candidate
for describing what's "different" about someone touched by genuine higher-dimensional contact, or about a
body immediately after death vs. immediately before.

THE BULK
Real modern physics term (Randall/Randall-Sundrum). The larger higher-dimensional space our own universe (a
"brane") may be floating within. Reads naturally as a genuine proper noun in-world — "the Bulk" — no
adaptation needed.

BRANE / 3-BRANE
Real modern physics term. A lower-dimensional "slice" that ordinary matter and forces (except gravity) are
physically stuck to. Could extend naturally to describing Tepenia itself, or the whole material universe, as
"our brane" in more esoteric/scholarly registers of the religion.

MULTIVERSE (precise sense)
Randall's own precise definition: specifically a scenario with more than one brane, weakly or
non-communicating. Worth preserving this precise sense distinctly from the looser pop-culture usage if the
term ever comes up in dialogue — the religion's own scholars would likely be pedantic about the distinction.

COSMIC STRINGS
Real hypothesized objects — relic threads from the earliest moments of the universe, potentially stretching
across the entire observable universe, searched for via gravitational lensing. A real "ancient thread
running through everything" image, ready-made.

COSMIC CRYSTALLOGRAPHY
Real proposed method (Lachièze-Rey, Lehoucq, Luminet, 1996) for detecting whether the universe "wraps
around" on itself — you'd see the same galaxy repeated at regular distances in every direction. A strong
name for an actual in-world observational discipline/vocation (see "the Watchers" in Extrapolations_2).

CIRCLES IN THE SKY
Real proposed method (Cornish, Spergel, Starkman, Weeks) — same idea as cosmic crystallography, applied to
the Cosmic Microwave Background instead of galaxies. Matching temperature-pattern circles would appear twice
in the sky if the universe wraps around. Also a strong candidate name for a specific rite, meditation, or
observational practice — literally "reading the sky for its own echo."

COSMIC FORGETFULNESS
Real term (physicist Martin Bojowald) for the loss of information/memory across a "Big Bounce" — our
universe potentially being the rebound of a prior, now-inaccessible universe. Strong candidate as the proper
name for the Cyclical denomination's own central doctrine or its founding text/teaching.

MAGIC DOORS
Rucker's own term (not a real physics term, but a real author's own coinage) for a wormhole-like connective
passage between two separate lower-dimensional universes — built by joining a "flap" cut from each,
ordinary-looking from a safe vantage, lethal ("Nothingness") if strayed from. Strong candidate for naming a
specific sacred/forbidden threshold location, shrine, or liminal space in-world.

"IT IS NEITHER [MADNESS NOR HELL]... IT IS KNOWLEDGE; IT IS THREE DIMENSIONS."
Direct quote, Flatland (Abbott). The single most reusable scriptural-register line found in the whole
research pass — reframes contact with the higher-dimensional as gnosis, not affliction. Could be adapted
almost verbatim into an in-world equivalent ("It is neither madness nor curse. It is Knowledge.") for a holy
text, a companion's own testimony, or a funeral/comfort formula.

"THE GOSPEL OF THE [X] DIMENSIONS" / "APOSTLE"
Direct register from Flatland's own Sphere character, who describes his own mission in exactly these terms.
Real scriptural vocabulary already sitting in a public-domain source, not invented — a strong template for
however this religion's own founding-teacher figure(s) might be described by later adherents.
